WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.436 --> 00:00:17.236
blinked at Winnie.

2
00:00:17.256 --> 00:00:19.838
"Uh, I don't get it, Winnie.

3
00:00:20.238 --> 00:00:22.860
How can we possibly find Pedro's treasure?

4
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:26.321
The treasure map is gone, remember?

5
00:00:26.782 --> 00:00:30.464
And Pedro buried that treasure chest a really long time ago."

6
00:00:32.536 --> 00:00:36.339
"That's exactly why we might be able to find it," Winnie said.

7
00:00:36.359 --> 00:00:40.503
"Because everyone else gave up looking a long time ago."

8
00:00:40.523 --> 00:00:44.106
"Good point," Mog agreed.

9
00:00:44.126 --> 00:00:46.268
"I think it's a good idea."

10
00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:53.094
Ben and his friends lowered their voices as they joined the other monsters in the lunch line.

11
00:00:53.114 --> 00:00:56.356
"I don't know, Winnie," Waldo said.

12
00:00:56.376 --> 00:00:59.339
"It sounds a little crazy, if you ask me.

13
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.221
It's like looking for a needle in a haystack—pretty much impossible."

14
00:01:06.602 --> 00:01:12.123
Plop! A cafeteria troll dropped a serving of toad toes onto Ben's tray.

15
00:01:12.143 --> 00:01:16.205
"Ugh." He made a face.

16
00:01:16.225 --> 00:01:19.666
"They're serving cold toad toes again?"

17
00:01:19.686 --> 00:01:23.447
"Yeah," Mog said.

18
00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:27.888
"That's all we ever get now—the cafeteria oven is broken."

19
00:01:29.236 --> 00:01:33.639
"So is the dishwasher," Ben said, eyeing stacks of dirty trays.

20
00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:39.062
"Well, I think Winnie's right," Gaby chimed in.

21
00:01:39.082 --> 00:01:42.224
"Detectives find missing stuff all the time.

22
00:01:42.764 --> 00:01:45.766
Maybe we can locate Pedro's treasure, even without the map."

23
00:01:46.946 --> 00:01:49.928
"I suppose we could try using magic," Waldo said.

24
00:01:49.948 --> 00:01:52.329
"What if I—ah-choo!"

25
00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:56.572
All the monsters in the lunch line ducked as fireworks burst overhead.

26
00:01:58.496 --> 00:02:02.039
"Hey, Waldo, you know the rule," a ghost said.

27
00:02:02.059 --> 00:02:04.800
"No spells in the lunchroom!"

28
00:02:05.721 --> 00:02:07.682
Gaby gave Waldo a sympathetic look.

29
00:02:07.703 --> 00:02:10.905
"I guess that sneezing spell hasn't worn off yet, huh?"

30
00:02:10.925 --> 00:02:14.607
"It's not a spell," Waldo insisted.

31
00:02:14.627 --> 00:02:17.589
"I told you, I just have a cold."

32
00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:20.011
"Sure you do," Gaby said.

33
00:02:20.571 --> 00:02:23.674
Waldo looked annoyed as she bent down to pat him on the shoulder.

34
00:02:24.694 --> 00:02:26.756
Winnie led the way to a quiet table.

35
00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:34.661
She gestured at the dripping ceiling and then at the floor, where a dozen buckets were lined up.

36
00:02:34.681 --> 00:02:39.004
"We have to do something.

37
00:02:39.485 --> 00:02:41.847
This school is becoming a disaster zone."

38
00:02:46.431 --> 00:02:50.214
A fish monster sat nearby, catching water drops in his mouth.

39
00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:55.498
"Some monsters seem to like it," Mog said with a shrug.

40
00:02:55.518 --> 00:03:02.236
"Well, if we did find the treasure," Winnie said, "we could use it to help fix up the

41
00:03:02.276 --> 00:03:06.520
school." "Conditions are getting pretty bad," Gaby said.

42
00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.383
"The kids over there are wearing winter coats and hats."

43
00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:14.607
"Yeah, because it's freezing in here," Ben said.

44
00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.348
"Just think.

45
00:03:16.869 --> 00:03:22.113
If we can find the treasure, we could make Monster Academy great again," Winnie said.

46
00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:25.416
"I'm sure we can do it," Gaby said.

47
00:03:26.316 --> 00:03:27.977
"We just need to think like detectives.

48
00:03:28.337 --> 00:03:30.417
They solve problems by using deduction."

49
00:03:31.618 --> 00:03:35.799
Mog shook up his carton of newt juice and took a big gulp.

50
00:03:37.359 --> 00:03:38.259
"What's deduction?"

51
00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.200
he asked.

52
00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:45.081
"It's examining clues and making smart guesses about what happened," Gaby said.

53
00:03:45.902 --> 00:03:47.102
Ben nodded slowly.

54
00:03:47.122 --> 00:03:51.603
"We might be able to find some clues about Pedro's treasure.

55
00:03:52.143 --> 00:03:53.704
But it won't be easy."

56
00:03:54.788 --> 00:03:59.850
Winnie put her hands over her ears as somebody started hammering on pipes somewhere nearby.

57
00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:06.611
"Sorry, but we don't have time to search for clues to make deductions," she said.

58
00:04:06.631 --> 00:04:09.652
"We need to find the treasure as soon as possible.

59
00:04:10.252 --> 00:04:13.333
Magic will be much easier—and faster."

60
00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:16.054
"I agree," Waldo said.

61
00:04:16.074 --> 00:04:22.956
"Magic is definitely the way to He pinched his nose to stop himself from sneezing again.

62
00:04:23.572 --> 00:04:26.594
His face turned red and smoke billowed out of his ears.

63
00:04:26.614 --> 00:04:30.616
"Deduction could be fast too," Gaby said.

64
00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:33.057
"Yeah," Mog said.

65
00:04:33.077 --> 00:04:37.420
"Detectives on TV always solve cases fast."

66
00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:41.262
"That's TV, Mog," Winnie said.

67
00:04:41.282 --> 00:04:45.964
"In real life, detective work is slow and painstaking.

68
00:04:46.224 --> 00:04:48.145
It takes a long time to figure out stuff."

69
00:04:49.306 --> 00:04:52.988
"Well, we could try being detectives," Mog said with a shrug.

70
00:04:53.504 --> 00:04:54.285
"It would be fun."

71
00:04:55.405 --> 00:04:56.866
"Yeah." Gaby nodded.

72
00:04:56.886 --> 00:04:58.387
"Lots of fun!"

73
00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:00.268
Waldo shook his head.

74
00:05:00.288 --> 00:05:03.309
"Magic would be faster and better."

75
00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:09.833
"I don't think so," Gaby said as Waldo sneezed again.

76
00:05:09.853 --> 00:05:13.715
"Especially since you have that, um, cold."

77
00:05:14.636 --> 00:05:16.357
Waldo cocked his head and looked at her.

78
00:05:16.377 --> 00:05:20.139
"Want to make a bet—magic versus detective work?"

79
00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:25.321
"Sure!" Gaby reached out her hand and grinned.

80
00:05:25.341 --> 00:05:29.824
"I'm confident that detective work will work better than magic."

81
00:05:30.705 --> 00:05:33.046
She shook hands with Waldo and then looked at the others.

82
00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.128
"Who's on my team?"

83
00:05:36.289 --> 00:05:38.110
"Me!" Mog said.

84
00:05:39.391 --> 00:05:40.872
Waldo looked at Winnie and Ben.

85
00:05:40.892 --> 00:05:44.414
"Well then, who wants to be on my team?"

86
00:05:46.315 --> 00:05:48.997
He hiccupped and more smoke came out of his ears.

87
00:05:49.017 --> 00:05:52.620
"I'll be on your team," Winnie said.

88
00:05:53.216 --> 00:05:54.998
"You might need some help with the magic."

89
00:05:56.380 --> 00:06:00.384
"Uh-oh Ben gulped as all his friends turned to look at him.

90
00:06:00.404 --> 00:06:04.428
"So, whose team are you on, Ben?"

91
00:06:04.849 --> 00:06:05.570
Gaby asked.

92
00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:09.674
She drummed her fingers on the table, waiting for him to answer.

93
00:06:09.694 --> 00:06:13.999
"Mine or Waldo's?"
